# One write fails in QEMU's block layer. The commit fails, `init` restarts the
# stack, and what was durable before it is there, with the failed work gone.
! panicked
< zosh$ 
# The first create after a mount commits, so it meets the failing write.
> write lost.txt in the failed commit\r
< init: storage failed
< zosh$ 
> cat hello.txt\r
< hello from the filesystem
< zosh$ 
> cat lost.txt\r
< zosh: cat: NotFound
< zosh$ 
> write after.txt the device works again\r
< zosh$ 
> sync\r
< zosh$ 
> cat after.txt\r
< the device works again
< zosh$ 
> poweroff\r
